    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d861">

                <pb facs="0928" n="1762" xml:id="pg1762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9089</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sulzer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Department of German <lb/> Interests IV 5</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received March 6.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my note of January 14,
                        1918,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d861-f1"/> enclosing text of a cablegram
                    regarding the extension of the blockade zone of January 31, 1917,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d861-f2"/> issued by the German Government on January 5, 1918 and
                    effective January 11, 1918, I now have the honor to enclose the original text of
                    this declaration, transmitted to this Legation by the Swiss Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>In this collection, I beg to draw your Excellency’s attention to the description
                    30 degrees 0 minutes north—26 degrees 0 minutes west. This description, due to
                    an error in the cablegram, was given in the text submitted to the Department of
                    State on January 14, 1918, as 30 degrees 0 minutes north—27 degrees 0 minutes
                    west.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hans Sulzer</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d861-a1.xml" xpointer="d861-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d861-f1" n="1" xml:id="d861-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d861-f2" n="2" xml:id="d861-f2-content">
                <p>For the German memorandum of Jan. 31, 1917, defining the blockade zone, see <ref
                        target="frus1917Supp01v01#pg_101">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1917, Supplement 1, pp.
                        101</ref>–<ref target="frus1917Supp01v01#pg_102">102</ref>. For declarations
                    of extension of this zone during 1917, see <ref
                        target="frus1917Supp01v01#pg_184">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, pp. 184</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus1917Supp01v01#pg_187">187</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
